		text = "Nobody is born a Fixer. You become one by passing the Hana Association's licensing exam: written questions about the Taboos, the Fingers and the Night, then a practical bout against an examiner. Pass it and you are a Grade 9 Fixer, the lowest grade there is.\n\nAfter every job a Fixer files a report, and Hana reads them all. Good work moves you up the scale toward Grade 1. Lies and unprofessional conduct can move you down. Higher grades get pricier jobs, and pricier jobs get more dangerous.\n\nEvery licensed Fixer must belong to an authorized organization: an Office or an Association. A one-person Office counts.",
